<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Iga Province</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Iga was an old province of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a>, in the hills south-east of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kyoto">Kyoto</a>, now the western part of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mie-prefecture">Mie Prefecture</a>. In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sengoku-period">Sengoku period</a> it had no strong lord and was governed by leagues of local warriors, famous as ninja. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oda-nobunaga">Oda Nobunaga</a> conquered it in 1581 in the Tenshō Iga War, and under the Tokugawa it belonged to the Tsu domain.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/iga-province.jpg" alt="Iga Province" width="320" height="335" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ash_Crow · CC BY 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Provinces_of_Japan-Iga.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
